I posted an analysis of monster generation at XL 14 vs. XL 30
a while back; the message ID is <slrnidma0l.5l1.aardvark@starfish.dhis.org>.

The short version is that although you're correct in that
keeping your XL low will not prevent high-difficulty monsters
from being generated, it /will/ reduce the probability that 
those high difficulty monsters will be generated.  The reason
is that as your XL increases, not only does the maximum 
level of monsters to be generated increase; so does the minimum
level of monsters to generate.  Because there are many more
low-level monsters than high-level monsters, if you keep your 
XL low then there are more monsters available to generate, and
therefore the probability of generating a high-level monster
goes down.

I focused on Archons (the usual monster that people are worried
about); it turns out that at XL 30 they are roughly twice as
likely to be generated than at XL 14.  That's a pretty 
substantial difference -- I think that the common belief that
keeping your XL low has no appreciable effect is wrong.

Now, you can make the argument that an XL 30 character will 
have much less trouble dealing with an Archon than an XL 14
character, but that's another can of worms.

